     "text": "You can ship a small music app in a single evening, and here is how the night goes. First, name one annoying problem, like finding a calm playlist without scrolling for ten minutes. Then look at how people already search: type a few words, press enter, and wait for a friendly reply from a seller. Copy that speed, not the screens, and your idea gets sharper. Next comes the look, a calm glass interface with a now playing pill, a tab bar, and one round search button. Keep every screen to one job, so nothing fights for attention. When it works on your phone, shipping is one command in the terminal. Push it, share one honest post, and let the first users tell you what to fix."
    }
   }
  ],
